# Shopware 6 Plugin Development

## Architecture Rules

- Follow Shopware's plugin architecture strictly
- Use services with dependency injection via `services.xml`
- Register event subscribers with the `kernel.event_subscriber` tag
- Use Shopware's SystemConfigService for plugin settings

## PHP Code Style

- Use `declare(strict_types=1)` in all PHP files
- Follow PSR-12 coding standard
- Add PHPDoc blocks for all classes and public methods
- Use type hints for all parameters and return types
- Namespace pattern: `Dropday\DropdayIntegration\`

## Configuration

- Define all settings in `Resources/config/config.xml`
- Use `DropdayIntegration.config.` prefix for config keys
- Support multi-language labels (en-GB, de-DE minimum)

## Event Handling

- Subscribe to state machine events for order sync
- Use proper event naming: `state_enter.order.state.{state}`
- Always load orders with required associations before processing

## API Integration

- Use cURL for HTTP requests to Dropday API
- Always include proper error handling
- Log API calls when debug mode is enabled
- Handle rate limits gracefully

## Administration (JavaScript/Vue)

- Follow Shopware admin component patterns
- Register modules in `src/Resources/app/administration/src/main.js`
- Use snippet files for translations
- Extend existing components with `Component.override()`
